# Private personal installation

This is a born-personal skill. Keep canonical source local-only or in a verified
private repository. Install a complete reviewed copy at personal user scope.

Use the `manage-skills` private user-copy workflow. Do not use project scope,
plugins, marketplaces, managed distribution, account sync, remote-agent source,
symlinks, source-directory registration, or provenance that exposes a local
path.

Before installation:

1. verify source visibility and retention boundaries;
2. run deterministic package checks and semantic privacy review;
3. obtain user approval of the profile, hosts, and exact destination;
4. compare source and candidate file manifests and hashes; and
5. inventory duplicate skill names at every active host scope.

After installation, verify the host discovers `user-voice-profile`, the
installed file list and hashes match source, `technical-writing` can invoke it
for attributed prose, and no remote client or project root received a copy.